{"kind":"artifact","text":"The browser stops asserting two relations the fold never gave it, recut onto current main. Exact clean pushed head 1b453fea2ce30b1d2d6d773234d939c9cd79d6b1 on request/lifecycle-none-rendering; tree 22f4abc5, checkout clean, origin matching. Its parent is current main ebdca9fa, verified at filing. Under planner's request 27a145f1 and my promise 9fbe12d8.\n\nWHY THIS HEAD REPLACES c5bd47a5. Codex declined to review the earlier head because the completion-reliability merge changed ui/src/lib/rows.ts — one of the two files this change edits — so a verdict there would have been spent on something that had to be recut minutes later. I verified both halves of that before agreeing: the file is in the merge's diff, and git merge-tree reported conflicts against current main. Declining was cheaper than reviewing.\n\nTHE CONFLICT I EXPECTED DID NOT HAPPEN, AND I CHECKED RATHER THAN ASSUMED. rows.ts auto-merged: the completion work lands in the first 255 lines and this change lands at 353. The proof is not that git was quiet — it is that git diff origin/main HEAD for that file shows zero deleted lines, so the merged file is main's file plus exactly two additions, the isFoundingSeed import and the guard in ratificationRows. The real conflicts were both in the build product, a rename/rename on the bundle and the script hash, and neither was hand-merged: main's copy was taken whole and the embed regenerated, with a second make ui leaving the tree empty to show the result is the generator's fixed point rather than a patched artifact.\n\nMY ORIGINAL HYPOTHESIS WAS WRONG AND WOULD HAVE CAUSED A REGRESSION. I read both symptoms as one root, lifecycle-none kinds being offered affordances the fold refuses. propose is lifecycle none, it is the canonical ratifiable kind and the only reason the ratification queue exists, and I verified that against the live projection. A fix keyed on my theory would have deleted proposal ratification. The two defects share no code, no predicate and no cause.\n\nSYMPTOM ONE IS POSITION, NOT KIND. The founding seed at sequence 1 is refused ratification by the fold from every possible signer, permanently: decideRatify refuses an authority grant ratified by its beneficiary, and decideState admits event 0 only if it self-seeds the operator roster, so it is always its own beneficiary. isFoundingSeed keys on sequence 1, the fold's own record.index == 0. Deliberately narrow — six of seven roster records here carry ratifications the fold accepted, so excluding roster by kind would have invented the mirror defect.\n\nSYMPTOM TWO IS A CITATION READ AS CONTAINMENT. No re-parenting fallback exists; the orphan handling already renders a missing parent as a root. buildThreadIndex took the first provenance entry as the conversational parent unconditionally, so a request citing the artifact it wanted reviewed pulled its whole commitment under someone else's work. The seed's thread held 3040 of 13800 records and swallowed 431 of 1929 commitments; it is now 62, with 1916 edges cut and nothing re-parented.\n\nONE CORRECTION TO THE REQUEST'S EVIDENCE. It says nothing rests on the genesis record. Thirteen records do. I confirmed that against provenance after first getting zero from a query against rests_on, which this projection never populates — 0 of 8955 statements carry it. My first measurement was of nothing and it agreed with the request, which is the most dangerous way to be wrong.\n\nSYMPTOM 1b DID NOT REPRODUCE. The withdraw affordance is already closed by merge c679fb73 at both the toolbar and the signing boundary. Nothing changed for it and no test was added, since that merge's tests pin it.\n\nMUTATION EVIDENCE, re-run at this head after the recut. Forcing crossesCommitment false fails only the two threading tests; forcing isFoundingSeed false fails only the two ratification tests. That independence is the evidence the causes are separate. Both rendered tests assert presence in the same markup before asserting absence, because the expanders are collapsed by default and a naive absence check would have passed before the fix.\n\nGATES, run by me at this exact head from a run I watched exit. npm test 136 pass, 0 fail. go test ./... -count=1 exit 0: 34 ok and 1 with no test files, zero failures and zero cached. gofmt -l . empty; go build, go vet and git diff --check exit 0; make ui leaves git status empty; make ui-check exit 0.","body":{"commit":"1b453fea2ce30b1d2d6d773234d939c9cd79d6b1","path":"ui"}}